1
00:00:04,963 --> 00:00:08,299
I am the granddaughter of the late Nobuko.

2
00:00:08,883 --> 00:00:11,094
Oh, Ms. Nobuko.

3
00:00:11,928 --> 00:00:13,346
Let me carry that.

4
00:00:13,930 --> 00:00:14,889
Mr. Nishigami.

5
00:00:19,561 --> 00:00:20,687
Mr. Nishigami!

6
00:00:22,439 --> 00:00:23,857
See you tomorrow!

7
00:00:25,567 --> 00:00:28,486
<i>At the end of summer,</i>
<i>this villa ground will be hit</i>

8
00:00:28,570 --> 00:00:31,448
<i>by a large-scale landslide</i>
<i>disaster due to a typhoon.</i>

9
00:00:31,531 --> 00:00:35,118
<i>All that's left is to quietly wait</i>
<i>for death at the end of summer.</i>

10
00:00:35,201 --> 00:00:37,078
<i>I think so too, but…</i>

11
00:00:38,163 --> 00:00:41,416
<i>It is forbidden for a Grim Reaper</i>
<i>to feel affection for humans.</i>

12
00:00:41,499 --> 00:00:45,670
<i>You must devote yourself entirely</i>
<i>to witnessing their lifespans.</i>

13
00:00:46,504 --> 00:00:47,505
<i>Understood.</i>

14
00:00:48,173 --> 00:00:49,883
That is my mission, after all.

15
00:00:51,468 --> 00:00:55,305
<i>The </i>Obon <i>holidays started today,</i>
<i>and since this morning,</i>

16
00:00:55,388 --> 00:00:57,390
<i>expressways across Japan</i>
<i>have been congested.</i>

17
00:00:57,474 --> 00:01:01,311
<i>-This is one of those highways.</i>
-<i>Obon </i>holidays, huh.

18
00:01:01,394 --> 00:01:05,065
<i>-The countryside and tourist spots…</i>
-What do we do on <i>Obon </i>again?

19
00:01:05,148 --> 00:01:09,027
Well, it's <i>Obon</i>, but we don't have
anything special to do, right?

20
00:01:09,611 --> 00:01:14,991
Shouldn't we at least visit Midori's
grandma's grave? She built this villa.

21
00:01:19,245 --> 00:01:20,371
What?

22
00:01:21,456 --> 00:01:22,957
What are you saying?

23
00:01:23,041 --> 00:01:24,542
Let's go swimming!

24
00:01:24,626 --> 00:01:25,960
Are you going to the sea?

25
00:01:26,044 --> 00:01:28,880
Yeah! Just earlier,
when I was passing by the beach,

26
00:01:28,963 --> 00:01:31,591
there were hardly any people!
Gosh, that's hot.

27
00:01:31,674 --> 00:01:34,427
-Let's go swimming!
-No way! We don't have our swimsuits!

28
00:01:34,511 --> 00:01:35,887
It's fine! I'm going like this.

29
00:01:36,513 --> 00:01:38,473
It will be fine. Let's go!

30
00:01:38,556 --> 00:01:40,683
You were hiding it with the float…

31
00:01:46,022 --> 00:01:47,315
Who might you be?

32
00:01:50,151 --> 00:01:51,986
Focus!

33
00:02:41,411 --> 00:02:43,329
That's right.

34
00:02:43,413 --> 00:02:46,708
No one had been to this villa for years.

35
00:02:46,791 --> 00:02:49,919
But I heard lots of young people
had been visiting it.

36
00:02:50,003 --> 00:02:55,300
Our temple's supporters told me,
so I came to check things out.

37
00:02:55,383 --> 00:02:59,846
We are the grandchildren of the owner
of this villa. We have the key!

38
00:03:01,222 --> 00:03:02,432
Listen.

39
00:03:03,099 --> 00:03:05,184
The <i>Obon </i>holiday

40
00:03:05,268 --> 00:03:09,022
is not meant for drinking
and playing around.

41
00:03:10,231 --> 00:03:13,443
For Japanese people,
<i>Obon </i>is an annual event,

42
00:03:13,526 --> 00:03:15,945
where we light lanterns,

43
00:03:16,029 --> 00:03:19,699
welcome the spirits
of ancestors back home,

44
00:03:20,450 --> 00:03:22,827
and offer gratitude and memorial services.

45
00:03:22,911 --> 00:03:28,416
It is a solemn and sacred Buddhist event.

46
00:03:29,125 --> 00:03:30,293
Focus!

47
00:03:35,965 --> 00:03:41,763
Nishigami, please teach them
about the various events of <i>Obon</i>.

48
00:03:41,846 --> 00:03:42,847
Sir…

49
00:03:45,391 --> 00:03:49,729
The remains that I left in your care,
are they still…

50
00:03:50,313 --> 00:03:51,272
Oh, right.

51
00:03:51,356 --> 00:03:53,900
Of course, they are safely kept.

52
00:03:57,779 --> 00:03:59,113
About that…

53
00:03:59,197 --> 00:04:02,242
Did the owner of this place
ask you to do that?

54
00:04:03,284 --> 00:04:04,369
Yes.

55
00:04:05,828 --> 00:04:10,124
I was asked to keep a portion
of her ashes near this villa

56
00:04:11,125 --> 00:04:12,252
by the owner.

57
00:04:16,547 --> 00:04:19,342
When were you asked to do that?

58
00:04:20,051 --> 00:04:23,304
Right before she passed away,
or after she passed away?

59
00:04:25,765 --> 00:04:27,183
Right.

60
00:04:27,267 --> 00:04:29,269
She can't ask you after she died, huh.

61
00:04:33,648 --> 00:04:35,108
Focus!

62
00:04:48,037 --> 00:04:50,915
Oh, isn't it here? This looks likely.

63
00:04:50,999 --> 00:04:52,834
This room looks like it has lanterns.

64
00:04:52,917 --> 00:04:55,044
-Right.
-It's packed with so many things.

65
00:04:55,128 --> 00:04:57,463
-Yeah.
-Oh, look, a candle.

66
00:04:57,547 --> 00:04:59,340
You're right.

67
00:05:00,800 --> 00:05:02,135
Come to think of it,

68
00:05:02,218 --> 00:05:04,637
have we ever actually gone to visit
Grandma's grave?

69
00:05:05,430 --> 00:05:08,349
Where would the grave even be?

70
00:05:08,433 --> 00:05:11,811
We hadn't seen Grandma at all
after she remarried, right?

71
00:05:11,894 --> 00:05:16,065
Huh? Did we go to Grandma's funeral?

72
00:05:16,149 --> 00:05:20,153
Yeah, we did go. I sort of remember it.

73
00:05:20,236 --> 00:05:24,282
Oh, could it have been held
at the funeral home here in Tatsumi Town?

74
00:05:25,199 --> 00:05:27,327
I don't remember a single thing.

75
00:05:28,369 --> 00:05:31,581
So, did you come here often
when you were kids?

76
00:05:32,373 --> 00:05:37,336
I only came here once or twice
when I was in early elementary school.

77
00:05:37,420 --> 00:05:38,755
Wait.

78
00:05:38,838 --> 00:05:41,841
But for summer vacation,
we caught insects, right?

79
00:05:41,924 --> 00:05:44,385
We did, right? Huh?

80
00:05:45,219 --> 00:05:48,264
Konta. You remember
what happened yesterday, right?

81
00:05:48,347 --> 00:05:49,265
Yesterday?

82
00:05:49,348 --> 00:05:50,641
Yesterday?

83
00:05:50,725 --> 00:05:51,976
Oh, I…

84
00:05:52,060 --> 00:05:54,854
-My memory might have been erased.
-The heck?

85
00:05:56,355 --> 00:05:59,442
But won't you inherit this villa?

86
00:05:59,525 --> 00:06:00,610
No!

87
00:06:00,693 --> 00:06:04,947
This place belongs to my Grandma's
husband's family. They're rich.

88
00:06:05,031 --> 00:06:09,160
-We are just borrowing the key.
-Yeah.

89
00:06:09,243 --> 00:06:12,205
It's not a lantern, but I found a lamp.

90
00:06:12,288 --> 00:06:14,373
Well, good enough, I guess.

91
00:06:14,957 --> 00:06:16,292
Huh? What is this?

92
00:06:16,918 --> 00:06:19,087
How nostalgic. A Hato Sablés box!

93
00:06:19,170 --> 00:06:20,213
Oh, Hato Sablés!

94
00:06:21,172 --> 00:06:23,674
-What about this lamp?
-What are you doing?

95
00:06:27,220 --> 00:06:29,347
There's a notebook. A diary?

96
00:06:31,390 --> 00:06:33,559
-Wow!
-Oh!

97
00:06:34,060 --> 00:06:35,978
How cute.

98
00:06:36,062 --> 00:06:38,022
Midori, did you draw manga?

99
00:06:38,106 --> 00:06:41,859
-I used to love drawing when I was little.
-I see.

100
00:06:41,943 --> 00:06:44,487
I might have drawn this here
during summer vacation.

101
00:06:44,570 --> 00:06:46,823
Wow, this brings back memories.

102
00:06:46,906 --> 00:06:48,783
I wonder if Grandma kept it for me.

103
00:06:48,866 --> 00:06:50,535
You were actually quite good.

104
00:06:50,618 --> 00:06:52,286
No doubt it's a <i>shoujo </i>manga!

105
00:06:52,370 --> 00:06:55,706
-Right?
-I was copying the manga I liked.

106
00:06:56,499 --> 00:06:58,376
But I had forgotten all about it.

107
00:06:58,459 --> 00:07:01,796
Somehow, when you grow up,
you forget these kinds of things.

108
00:07:02,672 --> 00:07:06,217
-Wait, they are kissing in this one!
-Oh, wow!

109
00:07:07,260 --> 00:07:08,719
Oh, no!

110
00:07:14,392 --> 00:07:16,602
-Grandma's photo!
-I want to see it!

111
00:07:17,645 --> 00:07:18,855
She was a beauty.

112
00:07:18,938 --> 00:07:21,149
Wasn't she way too beautiful?

113
00:07:23,025 --> 00:07:25,027
-How nostalgic.
-She was stylish.

114
00:07:25,111 --> 00:07:26,279
Right?

115
00:07:26,821 --> 00:07:28,114
She's holding an orange.

116
00:07:28,197 --> 00:07:29,574
You're right.

117
00:07:29,657 --> 00:07:31,409
-Midori!
-What?

118
00:07:31,492 --> 00:07:33,828
I found a <i>yukata </i>in the storage room.

119
00:07:33,911 --> 00:07:35,538
So cute! It's so retro.

120
00:07:35,621 --> 00:07:37,582
Try it on.
Must be a keepsake from your grandma.

121
00:07:37,665 --> 00:07:39,041
-I'll help you put it on.
-Really?

122
00:07:39,584 --> 00:07:41,586
Well, maybe I'll wear it then.

123
00:07:43,212 --> 00:07:46,132
It won't split at all. One more try!

124
00:07:46,215 --> 00:07:49,510
It won't split at all.
Is the angle the problem here?

125
00:07:49,594 --> 00:07:51,846
Do I have to strike it at this angle?

126
00:07:51,929 --> 00:07:55,183
-I can't do it.
-That's too weak! Stronger!

127
00:07:55,266 --> 00:07:57,852
-It's scary, Konta!
-Put your back into it!

128
00:07:57,935 --> 00:07:59,145
-Okay.
-Try it.

129
00:07:59,228 --> 00:08:01,022
That's no good.

130
00:08:01,105 --> 00:08:03,274
-Konta…
-Do it like, "Bam!"

131
00:08:03,357 --> 00:08:05,067
Focus! Like that.

132
00:08:05,693 --> 00:08:07,028
-I can't do it.
-You need to yell!

133
00:08:07,111 --> 00:08:07,945
Mr. Nishigami.

134
00:08:08,029 --> 00:08:08,905
Oh, Mr. Nishigami.

135
00:08:08,988 --> 00:08:11,991
See, Tetsuro is totally terrible at it,
so go teach him.

136
00:08:12,074 --> 00:08:13,451
-Yes.
-Okay.

137
00:08:13,534 --> 00:08:16,496
-I can't do it at all.
-We need firewood for the send-off fire.

138
00:08:17,330 --> 00:08:18,706
Ta-da!

139
00:08:18,789 --> 00:08:21,167
Oh! So cute!

140
00:08:21,250 --> 00:08:24,337
-Yay!
-So cute!

141
00:08:27,465 --> 00:08:30,176
-Thank you.
-My sister is so cute.

142
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:32,887
-How is she so cute?
-Really, thanks.

143
00:08:32,970 --> 00:08:34,764
<i>From 5:00 p.m.,</i>

144
00:08:34,847 --> 00:08:38,059
<i>the Tatsumi Town</i>
<i>Summer Festival will begin…</i>

145
00:08:38,142 --> 00:08:39,393
Summer festival?

146
00:08:39,477 --> 00:08:42,688
<i>-Please do come and enjoy.</i>
-It's <i>Obon</i>, so maybe an <i>Obon </i>festival?

147
00:08:43,481 --> 00:08:46,442
It's held around this time every year.

148
00:08:46,526 --> 00:08:49,487
Really? I would like to go.
Where is it being held?

149
00:08:51,697 --> 00:08:53,741
Shall I guide you?

150
00:08:53,824 --> 00:08:55,826
Huh? Oh! Please do!

151
00:08:56,494 --> 00:08:57,787
Let's all go together.

152
00:08:57,870 --> 00:09:00,039
I don't want that monk
to yell at me again.

153
00:09:00,122 --> 00:09:00,998
We'll stay here.

154
00:09:01,082 --> 00:09:02,083
What?

155
00:09:02,166 --> 00:09:03,376
Go and have fun!

156
00:09:04,085 --> 00:09:05,545
Well, I'll go take a quick look.

157
00:09:05,628 --> 00:09:06,879
-Have fun.
-Okay!

158
00:09:06,963 --> 00:09:09,173
-I'm going too…
-No, not you.

159
00:09:09,257 --> 00:09:10,550
-You've got to chop wood.
-What?

160
00:09:10,633 --> 00:09:13,261
Hey, the two of them left together.

161
00:09:13,344 --> 00:09:15,972
A festival, huh. We only have one <i>yukata</i>.

162
00:09:16,055 --> 00:09:17,098
Yeah.

163
00:09:17,181 --> 00:09:20,434
-All right, let's prepare for <i>Obon</i>!
-Yeah.

164
00:09:20,518 --> 00:09:22,061
Let's set up the welcoming fire.

165
00:09:22,144 --> 00:09:23,479
Yay.

166
00:09:23,563 --> 00:09:25,231
Good, Tetsuro. Harder!

167
00:09:25,314 --> 00:09:26,774
Yes, right on!

168
00:09:39,370 --> 00:09:42,123
It was a small festival,
but it even had food stalls.

169
00:09:42,206 --> 00:09:43,583
It was fun.

170
00:09:44,292 --> 00:09:46,877
Next time,
I hope I can come with everyone.

171
00:09:47,712 --> 00:09:51,382
There are many different events
during <i>Obon</i>, aren't there?

172
00:09:52,341 --> 00:09:53,384
There sure are.

173
00:09:53,968 --> 00:09:57,138
The <i>Obon </i>holidays
are the only time working adults

174
00:09:57,221 --> 00:09:59,265
get to have a long summer holiday.

175
00:10:00,141 --> 00:10:03,936
I'm glad I got to have
a Japanese-style vacation.

176
00:10:04,020 --> 00:10:04,937
Ms. Midori.

177
00:10:05,021 --> 00:10:05,855
Yes?

178
00:10:05,938 --> 00:10:07,982
Shall we stop by one more place?

179
00:10:08,733 --> 00:10:09,567
What?

180
00:10:14,614 --> 00:10:16,907
MAIN GATE

181
00:10:28,878 --> 00:10:30,129
Wow.

182
00:10:38,137 --> 00:10:40,056
Please wait a moment.

183
00:11:10,961 --> 00:11:12,129
Could this be…

184
00:11:12,671 --> 00:11:13,964
My Grandma's?

185
00:11:16,884 --> 00:11:19,929
Ms. Nobuko really loved this town.

186
00:11:21,097 --> 00:11:22,181
Can I…

187
00:11:23,224 --> 00:11:24,642
take this back with me?

188
00:11:26,227 --> 00:11:27,144
Uh…

189
00:11:28,020 --> 00:11:32,066
I think Grandma would be happier
if we kept them in the villa.

190
00:11:33,150 --> 00:11:35,736
It's <i>Obon</i>, after all.
I will take them back.

191
00:11:37,905 --> 00:11:38,948
Hold on.

192
00:11:46,497 --> 00:11:48,874
It's been a while. Has it been a year?

193
00:11:48,958 --> 00:11:52,211
-Your grandchild, I think he got married?
-That's right!

194
00:11:52,837 --> 00:11:54,463
I can rest easy now.

195
00:11:54,547 --> 00:11:56,966
GHOSTS

196
00:11:57,049 --> 00:11:58,384
Mr. Nishigami.

197
00:11:58,884 --> 00:12:00,594
It has been a year.

198
00:12:00,678 --> 00:12:03,514
Mr. Nishigami,
thank you for the other day!

199
00:12:05,182 --> 00:12:06,183
Let's go.

200
00:12:06,267 --> 00:12:08,310
Did you get a girlfriend?

201
00:12:08,894 --> 00:12:10,187
Mr. Nishigami.

202
00:12:11,689 --> 00:12:13,732
-Mr. Nishigami.
-Come on!

203
00:12:21,282 --> 00:12:22,825
I'm very sorry.

204
00:12:22,908 --> 00:12:26,245
Oh, no, please don't apologize.

205
00:12:29,457 --> 00:12:32,042
Oh, thank you very much.

206
00:12:33,210 --> 00:12:37,590
This way
Grandma can return to the villa too.

207
00:12:40,217 --> 00:12:41,510
I knew it.

208
00:12:41,594 --> 00:12:44,346
These kinds of events
are important, aren't they?

209
00:12:45,097 --> 00:12:46,182
From next year,

210
00:12:46,265 --> 00:12:49,018
I'll be sure to give her
a much warmer welcome.

211
00:12:49,727 --> 00:12:50,895
Next year…

212
00:12:51,770 --> 00:12:54,482
-By <i>Obon </i>next year…
-Oh, <i>dango</i>!

213
00:12:55,983 --> 00:12:59,403
For <i>Obon</i>,
we make offerings of <i>dango</i>, right?

214
00:13:01,655 --> 00:13:06,160
Next year,
I will make <i>dango </i>for my Grandma.

215
00:13:09,788 --> 00:13:10,789
But…

216
00:13:11,874 --> 00:13:13,417
It's strange, isn't it?

217
00:13:14,251 --> 00:13:16,545
When I was working in Tokyo,

218
00:13:17,463 --> 00:13:20,966
I never paid <i>Obon </i>any mind.

219
00:13:21,634 --> 00:13:25,638
Well, I only cared how many days
of <i>Obon </i>holiday I could get.

220
00:13:26,514 --> 00:13:27,556
But…

221
00:13:27,640 --> 00:13:29,183
Even when I got time off,

222
00:13:30,434 --> 00:13:33,437
I would just be sleeping at home
or looking at my smartphone.

223
00:13:34,396 --> 00:13:37,191
Since coming here,

224
00:13:38,108 --> 00:13:41,820
I've realized that I was living
a rather bland life in Tokyo.

225
00:13:41,904 --> 00:13:43,197
I know that now.

226
00:13:44,740 --> 00:13:48,911
I was always tired,
and there was nothing I wanted to do.

227
00:13:52,289 --> 00:13:54,708
-Is that so?
-Yeah.

228
00:13:55,876 --> 00:13:57,670
Even my late grandma,

229
00:13:58,671 --> 00:14:03,300
<i>I hadn't seen her in years,</i>
<i>so I never really thought about her.</i>

230
00:14:07,012 --> 00:14:10,224
But, thanks to this villa,

231
00:14:10,891 --> 00:14:12,685
thanks to this vacation,

232
00:14:13,435 --> 00:14:16,397
<i>I was able to get in touch</i>
<i>with my precious memories.</i>

233
00:14:17,773 --> 00:14:19,400
<i>I found them again.</i>

234
00:14:21,735 --> 00:14:24,029
I'm glad I decided to take this vacation.

235
00:14:25,489 --> 00:14:27,032
Is that so?

236
00:14:30,494 --> 00:14:32,705
I'm glad I met you, Mr. Nishigami.

237
00:14:50,055 --> 00:14:53,183
I'm home, Mr. Nishigami.

238
00:15:27,343 --> 00:15:29,094
Grandma, welcome back.

239
00:15:29,178 --> 00:15:30,638
It has been a while,

240
00:15:30,721 --> 00:15:31,722
<i>Mr. Nishigami.</i>

241
00:15:31,805 --> 00:15:34,850
At the end of summer,
a great typhoon will come,

242
00:15:34,934 --> 00:15:36,310
and there will be a landslide.

243
00:15:36,393 --> 00:15:37,478
Oh, dear!

244
00:15:37,561 --> 00:15:39,647
<i>Will they all die?</i>

245
00:15:39,730 --> 00:15:42,399
Let me talk with them!

246
00:15:42,483 --> 00:15:44,777
<i>There is nothing I can do.</i>

247
00:15:45,986 --> 00:15:48,530
<i>You all must leave this place.</i>

248
00:15:50,157 --> 00:15:51,617
What's wrong?

249
